# SmartDNS force-foreign.conf
# Purpose: Fix domains where VPN exit IP triggers server-side redirect loops.
#
# DIAGNOSIS METHOD (Playwright redirect capture):
#   1. Capture redirect chain in browser
#   2. Identify the loop pattern
#   3. Check if CN IP direct access serves content (no redirect back)
#   4. Add address override if CN IP is in bypass_ipv4 AND serves content directly
#
# Microsoft Bing: ERR_TOO_MANY_REDIRECTS
#   Root cause (confirmed by Exa research + Playwright capture):
#   - Microsoft detects commercial VPN exit IPs as "China VPN users"
#   - www.bing.com (VPN IP) -> 302 -> cn.bing.com
#   - cn.bing.com (VPN IP, global edge) -> 301 -> www.bing.com?mkt=zh-CN -> loop
#   Fix: force BOTH to 202.89.233.101 (CN bypass IP, DIRECT path).
#   With CN ISP IP: www.bing.com -> cn.bing.com (1 redirect) -> serves content.
#   TLS verified: cert at 202.89.233.101 has SAN *.bing.com + www.bing.com.
#   Reference: Clash Verge #1702, SearxNG #2193, V2EX t/927161
address /bing.com/202.89.233.101
address /cn.bing.com/202.89.233.101
